Both of these components use "transducers" which are apparently devices that converts energy from one form to another. For example, a physical input like pressure from pressing down on the Brakes will turn into an electrical signal.

The brake pressure sensor are "pressure transducers" that operate between -20 and 135+ degrees C(in Fahrenheit that's about -4 to 275 degrees), and the one linked in GitHub has a pressure range of 0-2000 PSI.

The current sensor is also a transducer that measures both AC and DC currents. It converts the current it is measuring into an output signal that most systems can read. 

